      "id": 1,
      "text": "Auburntown was once called Poplar Stand because of abundant poplar trees before being renamed after Auburn, New York.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburntown%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town incorporated in 1949, giving it official municipal status within Cannon County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburntown%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Auburntown sits at 35°56′59″N 86°05′45″W, placing it in the heart of Tennessee’s Highland Rim.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburntown%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The AuburnTown Historical Society, founded in 1982, preserves local heritage in a museum and library on Courthouse Square.",
